      "metadata": {
        "key": "winsheet.newtab",
        "segment": "sheet-host",
        "name": "winsheet.newtab",
        "kind": "native",
        "description": "(state, host) - the '+' on a worksheet window's tab strip: genesis-create a BLANK 10x10 sheet, mint it as its own private closure, tab it into the clicked window (win.geom[new].host=host), and bundle the host clique so the new tab shares memory with its host."
      },
      "locked": true
    },
    {
      "key": "winsheet.syncBundles",
      "celType": "LockedLambdaCel",
      "metadata": {
        "key": "winsheet.syncBundles",
        "segment": "sheet-host",
        "name": "winsheet.syncBundles",
        "kind": "native",
        "description": "(state) - make SEEDED tab relationships grant shared memory like a runtime drop does: scan win.geom and bundleSegments each {host, tabs...} clique, so a sheet minted private-get (a closure) can read its host's cels when win.geom seeds seg.host (e.g. turtlecharts tabbed into turtles reads turtles!). Idempotent; the host calls it after the desktop genesis materializes."
      },
      "locked": true
